In October 2025, while the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 23|previous series]] was in production, hosts [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] announced their departures from the show.<ref>{{cite web |title=Tess Daly and Claudia Winkleman to leave Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cz0x1lr7j92o |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=23 October 2025}}</ref> In a joint statement, they said "We have loved working as a duo and hosting ''Strictly Come Dancing'' has been an absolute dream. We were always going to leave together and now feels like the right time."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Duggins |first1=Alexi |title=Claudia Winkleman and Tess Daly to leave Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/oct/23/claudia-winkleman-tess-daly-to-leave-strictly-come-dancing |website=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=23 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Claudia Winkleman and Tess Daly to leave Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.thetimes.com/uk/media/article/tess-daly-claudia-winkleman-leave-strictly-come-dancing-950r2r0qb |website=[[The Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=23 October 2025 |archive-date=26 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260426163830/https://www.thetimes.com/uk/media/article/tess-daly-claudia-winkleman-leave-strictly-come-dancing-950r2r0qb |url-status=live }}</ref> The [[BBC]] subsequently began holding auditions for new presenters, who subsequently held "chemistry tests" prior to the decision.<ref name="mensah rt">{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=9 Strictly Come Dancing presenter contenders tipped to be in auditions {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-presenters-auditions-chemistry-tests-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |archive-date=21 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260421054528/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-presenters-auditions-chemistry-tests-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Several presenters and former contestants were rumoured to become new presenters, including former ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' host and [[Strictly Come Dancing series 3|series 3]] contestant [[Zoe Ball]], then ''It Takes Two'' host and [[Strictly Come Dancing series 20|series 20]] contestant [[Fleur East]], former ''It Takes Two'' host [[Rylan Clark]], [[Strictly Come Dancing series 9|series 9]] contestant and ''[[The One Show]]'' presenter [[Alex Jones (Welsh presenter)|Alex Jones]], [[Strictly Come Dancing series 21|series 21]] contestant [[Angela Scanlon]], [[Strictly Come Dancing series 12|series 12]] contestant [[Alison Hammond]] and [[Strictly Come Dancing series 23|series 23]] contestant [[La Voix (drag queen)|La Voix]], as well as [[Bradley Walsh]], [[Tom Allen (comedian)|Tom Allen]] and [[Emma Willis]].<ref name="mensah rt" /> In May 2026, Ball confirmed she had auditioned as presenter, but was rejected for the role, stating that she had "worked through the 7 stages of rejection and grief".<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Zoe Ball confirms she will not be show's new presenter |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/czx2w0wz7nro |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=12 May 2026 |archive-date=13 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260513073026/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/czx2w0wz7nro |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Zoe Ball loses out on Strictly presenting role |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2026/05/12/zoe-ball-lost-out-strictly-come-dancing-presenting-role/ |website=[[Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |archive-date=13 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260513111243/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2026/05/12/zoe-ball-lost-out-strictly-come-dancing-presenting-role/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Clark, [[Sara Cox]], [[Clara Amfo]], and [[Siân Welby]] all confirmed later that they had participated in screen tests for the roles, along with several others.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-20 |title=Rylan shares joke video of himself crying inconsolably after losing out on Strictly |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-presenters-new-rylan-bbc-b2980121.html |access-date=2026-05-20 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Sansome |first=Jessica |date=2026-05-19 |title=Sara Cox opens up bid for Strictly host job after BBC Radio 2 Breakfast role |url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/tv/sara-cox-opens-up-bid-33975811 |access-date=2026-05-20 |website=Manchester Evening News |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Fabbro |first=Lauren Del |last2=Reporter |first2=Press Association Entertainment |date=2026-09-21 |title=Clara Amfo secretly auditioned to host Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.irishnews.com/entertainment/clara-amfo-secretly-auditioned-to-host-strictly-come-dancing-4PLGT36QCJMCRIAYONC237S4VE/ |access-date=2026-09-21 |website=The Irish News |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mensah |first=Katelyn |title=This Morning star says Strictly host audition process was "gruelling" {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/sian-welby-strictly-come-dancing-host-audition-newsupdate/ |access-date=2026-10-02 |website=www.radiotimes.com |language=en-GB}}</ref> East also confirmed that she would not be presenting the series, stating that she felt she would be acceptable with "not doing it or not being considered for the job", but said she was "kind of bothered."<ref>{{cite web |title=Another Strictly Come Dancing host frontrunner rules themselves out: "I'm kind of bothered" |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a71295962/strictly-come-dancing-host-fleur-east/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=13 May 2026 |archive-date=13 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260513220217/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a71295962/strictly-come-dancing-host-fleur-east/ |url-status=live }}</ref> 

On 19 May 2026, it was confirmed that Emma Willis, [[Josh Widdicombe]] and [[Johannes Radebe]] would present the series. Widdicombe previously appeared as a contestant on the [[List of Strictly Come Dancing specials#2024|2024 Christmas Special]], while Radebe had appeared as a professional dancer since the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 16|sixteenth series]]. It marks the first time that the show had been regularly presented by three hosts.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2026 presenting trio Emma Willis, Johannes Radebe and Josh Widdicombe unveiled |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/strictly-come-dancing-2026-presenters-confirmed-emma-willis-johannes-radebe-josh-widdicombe |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=19 May 2026 |language=en}}</ref> In August 2026, it was announced on Willis' [[BBC Radio 2]] show that series 20 contestant [[Ellie Taylor]] would become the new presenter of the spin-off show ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'', replacing East and [[Janette Manrara]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing announces new It Takes Two, hosted by Ellie Taylor |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/strictly-come-dancing-new-it-takes-two-ellie-taylor |website=[[BBC]] |language=en}}</ref> It was later revealed that comedian Abi Clarke and series 20 contestant [[Tyler West]] would host ''Strictly: Lights Up'', a new spin-off series which streams on BBC iPlayer after every Sunday results show. Clarke also hosted weekly training room episodes, where she visited different couples in rehearsals.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-lights-off-spin-off-newsupdate/|title=BBC confirms new Strictly spin-off Lights|first=Morgan|last=Cormack|website=www.radiotimes.com|date=21 September 2026|access-date=21 September 2026}}</ref> [[CBBC]] introduced ''Strictly Pro Dance Off'', a dance tutorial and competition series featuring the professional dancers that is also broadcast as a segment on Saturday mornings during ''[[Saturday Mash-Up!]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/cbbc-new-professional-dance-tutorial-series-strictly-come-dancing/|title=CBBC brings Strictly sparkle to young audiences with new professional dance tutorial series|website=www.bbc.co.uk|date=17 September 2026|accessdate=4 October 2026}}</ref>

=== Professional dancers ===
In March 2026, it was reported that several professional dancers would be leaving the show.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=''Strictly'' tipped for even more pro dancer changes as another 'dropped' |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/nadiya-bychkova-strictly-come-dancing-2026-axed-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |archive-date=5 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260405154535/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/nadiya-bychkova-strictly-come-dancing-2026-axed-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Revealed: The savage way ''Strictly'' is 'picking' which professional dancers stay on the show |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a70830742/strictly-tiktok-professional-dancers-axed/ |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=24 March 2026 |archive-date=28 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260328182001/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a70830742/strictly-tiktok-professional-dancers-axed/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Later that month, [[Karen Hauer]], the show's longest serving female professional who had appeared since the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 10|tenth series]], confirmed her departure and said that it was "the right time" to leave the show and focus on other projects.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'': Karen Hauer to leave show after 14 years |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/articles/cdrmjxxdg36o |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=21 March 2026 |archive-date=23 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260323052537/https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/articles/cdrmjxxdg36o |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly Come Dancing''{{'s}} Karen Hauer quits show after 14 years |url=https://www.itv.com/news/2026-03-21/strictly-come-dancings-karen-hauer-quits-show-after-14-years |website=[[ITV News]] |access-date=14 May 2026 }}</ref> [[Nadiya Bychkova]], who had served as a professional since the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 15|fifteenth series]] was also announced to be leaving the show, and said in a statement that the show had "allowed [her] to discover new sides of [herself], develop new skills, and evolve as an artist in ways [she would] always be grateful for."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' 2026 confirms major change for professional dancer |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/nadiya-bychkova-strictly-come-dancing-exit-confirmed-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |archive-date=6 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260506143635/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/nadiya-bychkova-strictly-come-dancing-exit-confirmed-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly'' star Nadiya Bychkova confirms exit from BBC series amid ongoing overhaul |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-nadiya-bychkova-exit-bbc-karen-hauer-b2945914.html |website=[[The Independent]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |language=en |date=26 March 2026}}</ref> [[Luba Mushtuk]], who joined the show during the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 16|sixteenth series]], also confirmed her departure, and thanked the show for "the amazing opportunity and unforgettable memories" adding that "it [had] truly meant the world to [her]".<ref>{{cite web |title=Luba Mushtuk Becomes Latest ''Strictly'' Pro To Leave Show Ahead Of This Year's Series |url=https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/luba-mushtuk-leaves-strictly-come-dancing_uk_69c68152e4b041837420605d |website=[[HuffPost]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |language=en |date=27 March 2026 |archive-date=28 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260328082526/https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/luba-mushtuk-leaves-strictly-come-dancing_uk_69c68152e4b041837420605d |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' hit by another exit as a third professional quits |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/culture/strictly-come-dancing-luba-mushtuk-b2946985.html |website=[[The Independent]] |access-date=29 March 2026 |language=en |date=27 March 2026 |archive-date=28 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260328084102/https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/culture/strictly-come-dancing-luba-mushtuk-b2946985.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Michelle Tsiakkas]], who joined during the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 20|twentieth series]], subsequently confirmed she had been dismissed from the show. Tsiakkas said she was told via a [[Zoom (software)|Zoom]] call that her contract had not been renewed and said that her "dream was shattered", as well as that she was "grieving for her job".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' star reveals upset after being axed from show |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-michelle-tsiakkas-dropped-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026}}</ref> She ultimately decided not to participate in ''Strictly: The Professionals'' tour.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly'' professional quits 2026 tour after being ‘axed’ from series |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-2026-michelle-tsiakkas-professionals-tour-b2938450.html |website=[[The Independent]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |language=en |date=14 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title="Finding the light again": ''Strictly'' pro speaks out about being ‘axed’ from the show and quitting live tour |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a70733053/strictly-pro-dancer-on-being-axed-quitting-tour/ |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=13 March 2026 |archive-date=20 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260320110821/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a70733053/strictly-pro-dancer-on-being-axed-quitting-tour/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The following month, [[Gorka Márquez]], a professional since the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 14|fourteenth series]], was the final professional to confirm to be leaving the show, following his reduced role the previous series due to his commitments as a judge on the Spanish version of the show {{lang|es|Bailando con las estrellas}}.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' confirms exit of fan-favourite dancer after 10 years |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-gorka-marquez-exit-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |archive-date=6 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260506143915/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-gorka-marquez-exit-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Márquez said that being part of ''Strictly Come Dancing'' had been "so much more than just a professional opportunity", adding that "it allowed [him] to build a career from [his] passion", and that he would "forever be thankful."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Karasin |first1=Ekin |title=Gorka Marquez's surprising career move revealed after ''Strictly'' exit |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/gorka-marquez-career-move-strictly-come-dancing-b1280390.html |website=[[Evening Standard]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |language=en |date=29 April 2026 |archive-date=30 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260430083733/https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/gorka-marquez-career-move-strictly-come-dancing-b1280390.html |url-status=live }}</ref> 

In May 2026, the BBC confirmed that [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Julian Caillon]], [[Vito Coppola]], [[Amy Dowden]], [[Carlos Gu]], [[Katya Jones]], [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Nikita Kuzmin]], [[Lauren Oakley]], [[Jowita Przystał]], [[Johannes Radebe]], [[Aljaž Škorjanec]], [[Alexis Warr]], [[Kai Widdrington]] and [[Nancy Xu]] would all be returning for this series. Radebe was later confirmed to be co-presenting the show.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'': Five pros to leave the show as line-up confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c20214nnggdo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 May 2026 |date=6 May 2026 |archive-date=13 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260513113350/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c20214nnggdo |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Five pros to leave ''Strictly Come Dancing'' as full line-up confirmed |url=https://www.itv.com/news/2026-05-06/five-pros-to-leave-strictly-come-dancing-as-full-line-up-confirmed |website=[[ITV News]] |access-date=14 May 2026}}</ref> In July 2026, five new professional dancers were announced for the series: [[Aleksandra Isaeva]], [[Maddie Ingoldsby]], [[Mark Karmalita]], [[Lethabo Monametsi]] and [[Cristian Priori]].<ref>{{cite web |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' announces five new Pro Dancers |url=https://bbc.com/mediacentre/2026/strictly-come-dancing-new-pro-dancers |website=[[BBC Media Centre]]|access-date=25 July 2026}}</ref>

During the launch show, Neil Jones, Aleksandra Isaeva, Cristian Priori and Lethabo Monametsi did not receive a celebrity partner, while the rest were paired up, including new professionals Maddie Ingoldsby and Mark Karmalita.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-2026-pairs-confirmed-newsupdate/ |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' confirms pairings for revamped 2026 season |work=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=19 September 2026}}</ref>

==Couples==
On 10 June 2026, [[Lacey Turner]] was announced as the first contestant to be competing in the series.<ref>{{cite news |title=Lacey Turner is the first celebrity contestant confirmed for Strictly Come Dancing 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2026/strictly-come-dancing-lacey-turner |access-date=10 June 2026 |publisher=[[BBC Media Centre]]}}</ref> Following her withdrawal from the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 23|previous series]] prior to the first week due to an ankle injury, [[Dani Dyer]] was announced to be returning as a contestant for this series.<ref>{{cite web|title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms SECOND celebrity contestant – with past connection to the show|first=Laura Jane|last=Turner|work=[[Digital Spy]]|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a71556483/strictly-come-dancing-2026-second-celebrity-dani-dyer/|date=11 June 2026|access-date=11 June 2026}}</ref> Celebrity reveals continued over the next two months, before the line-up was completed on 12 August 2026.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly’s celebrity dancers – and everything else we know for 2026 |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2026/06/11/strictly-2026-line-up/ |website=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=12 June 2026}}</ref>

